    fix(cli): make `speclang new` emit a runnable project, not a machine-bound stub (UX-003)
    
    A scaffolded project declared devDependencies { "speclang": "file:/home/kara/SpecLang" }
    and no bin, so a stranger's `npm install` pointed at one machine's checkout and the
    documented next steps (speclang validate / generate) resolved to nothing.
    
    What changed (bin/speclang, the hand-written CLI source):
    - the generated package.json no longer carries the absolute `file:` dependency; the
      scaffold has no third-party dependencies at all
    - `speclang new` now emits scripts/speclang.cjs, a runtime-resolving shim: $SPECLANG_CLI
      override, then node_modules/speclang, then node_modules/.bin/speclang, then the CLI
      that generated the project; it fails loudly with the exact path when an override is wrong
    - generated npm scripts (validate/generate/start/build/test/dev) and the "Next steps"
      text now call the shim, and the text says `npm install` is optional
    
    Verification (real output):
    - npm run build -> exit 0
    - tests/cli/new-project-runnable.test.ts -> 8 passed (new test: shim resolution order,
      override rejection, generated scripts, no absolute path in the scaffold)
    - live: `speclang new demo` in a temp dir -> npm install --no-audit --no-fund exit 0 ->
      `node scripts/speclang.cjs validate` exit 0 with "Validation Summary: 1 files / Passed: 1"
